From: System Electronics
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: wait for clock and data lanes to be ready

Backport of "drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: Wait for Clk and Data Lanes to be
ready", patch 05 of the same upstream series, which has already been taken
into stable.

cdns_dsi_bridge_enable() raised VID_EN without ever checking that the
D-PHY clock and data lanes had finished their LP to HS transition. The
cover letter of the series states the requirement plainly: "This
controller requires to be enabled before the previous entity enables its
stream. It's a strict requirement which, if not followed, causes the
colors to 'shift' on the display."

On the Astrial H15 the display pipe violates that order in the other
direction: the Hailo DPI starts its scanout in the CRTC atomic_enable,
which the atomic helper runs before the bridge pre_enable where the D-PHY
is brought up. Waiting for the lanes here is the half of the fix that is
local to this driver and affordable now. The real fix is patches 10 to 14
of the same series, which reorder the bridge chain against the CRTC in
the atomic helper core, and is not backportable on this schedule.

The register bits already existed in our tree: MCTL_MAIN_STS, CLK_LANE_RDY
and DATA_LANE_RDY(l).

Local addition: measure and log how long the wait takes. readl_poll_timeout
only reports whether it expired, and the shape of the wait is itself the
diagnosis. A long first wait followed by short ones points at the ordering
inversion above; a wait that is always near zero means this patch is not
what fixed anything, and the credit belongs to the phy de-init patch.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
+#include <linux/ktime.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of_address.h>
 #include <linux/of_graph.h>
@@ -791,7 +792,11 @@
 	unsigned long tx_byte_period;
 	struct cdns_dsi_cfg dsi_cfg;
 	u32 tmp, reg_wakeup, div;
+	u32 status, lane_mask;
+	ktime_t phy_wait_start;
+	s64 phy_wait_us;
 	int nlanes;
+	int i, ret;
 
 	if (WARN_ON(pm_runtime_get_sync(dsi->base.dev) < 0))
 		return;
@@ -804,6 +809,25 @@
 	cdns_dsi_hs_init(dsi);
 	cdns_dsi_init_link(dsi);
 
+	/* Wait for clock and data lanes before enabling video, and log how long. */
+	lane_mask = CLK_LANE_RDY;
+	for (i = 0; i < nlanes; i++)
+		lane_mask |= DATA_LANE_RDY(i);
+
+	phy_wait_start = ktime_get();
+	ret = readl_poll_timeout(dsi->regs + MCTL_MAIN_STS, status,
+				 (status & lane_mask) == lane_mask,
+				 100, 500000);
+	phy_wait_us = ktime_us_delta(ktime_get(), phy_wait_start);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(dsi->base.dev,
+			"Timed Out: DSI-DPhy Clock and Data Lanes not ready after %lld us (MCTL_MAIN_STS 0x%08x, wanted 0x%08x)\n",
+			phy_wait_us, status, lane_mask);
+	else
+		dev_info(dsi->base.dev,
+			 "DSI-DPhy Clock and Data Lanes ready after %lld us\n",
+			 phy_wait_us);
+
 	writel(HBP_LEN(dsi_cfg.hbp) | HSA_LEN(dsi_cfg.hsa),
 	       dsi->regs + VID_HSIZE1);
 	writel(HFP_LEN(dsi_cfg.hfp) | HACT_LEN(dsi_cfg.hact),
